# Skill Wiring

Composition registry: select the domain owner through [INDEX](INDEX), then read only the relevant route below. Skill bodies own methods; this map owns composition. When adding/renaming/removing a skill, update its route and handoffs here. A route never grants launch, spending, signing, disclosure or implementation authority.

Installation boundary: this map intentionally binds capabilities to concrete skill identities. Individual bundles must remain usable without this map or sibling trees: describe required inputs, output/evidence, authority and absent-capability stops locally. A skill rename changes discovery/installation mappings, not unrelated operational workflows.

## Default Composition Rules

- Code-logic work defaults to `code-craft` unless a narrower skill owns the design dimension; it can support another primary as a design lens. Simple formatting/config/rename edits need no skill; otherwise prefer the narrowest owner.
- Non-trivial work requires `team-operating-model` alongside the domain owner before substantive execution; activation means a real primary plus separate worker with current evidence. Exclude trivial tasks first; unavailable permission/capability/evidence blocks affected work, never solo/simulated fallback.
- Specifications use only the needed owner: `brainstorming` product, `architecture-design` technical, `code-craft` behavior, `ui-ux` journeys/states; `doc-craft` presents established meaning. Start with [lightweight planning](working-principles/references/planning.md) when useful, not a PRD→TRD→BDD ladder. Research/specification does not authorize implementation.
- Preserve domain ownership on every handoff. Deep references are on demand; paths resolve from this skills directory. Project indexes retain core + used skills only. Management reporting uses `../docs/ai-augmented-project-setup-and-evolution.md` §9 for topics and an audience-appropriate ad-hoc template, not a dedicated skill.

## Cross-Cutting Contracts

### Direction Settlement (Cross-Cutting)

Consequential interpretation/design/trade-offs require an eligible proposal (objective/invariants, source facts, alternatives, recommendation, uncertainty) → **separate original-source validation**, including compatible earlier constraints and a disconfirmer → applicable authority (configured decision-support for in-scope choices, explicitly delegated architect decision, or user for reserved decisions). A decision tool cannot perform the independent validation. The deciding architect/user may validate only if not the proposer.

The architect decision job is bounded/read-only and receives originals, proposal, validation, authority boundary and question; returns the decision, reconciliation, conditions, uncertainty, change conditions or `INCOMPLETE`. The primary records the confirmed choice in existing task context and executes; it cannot self-ratify or override. Do not select a validator or authority to obtain a preferred answer. Missing roles block. Mechanically source-settled steps need no separate round. Safety/reserved approvals remain; this is decision ownership, not permission, team activation or a substitute for cross-family challenge.

### Decision Consultation (Cross-Cutting)

Use `decision-support` for meaningful autonomous next steps, recommendations before asking or worker continue/return uncertainty: gather evidence, consult an existing authorized capability through its actual harness contract, then return through the applicable authority. Skip trivial deterministic choices. Consultation is not fact gathering, delegation, independent review or hard-stop bypass; absence does not waive gates.

### Authorized Delivery and Persistent Work

`team-operating-model` owns delivery, deliberation and aggregate acceptance; matching domain skills own substance. Honor collaborative/HITL requests; authorized autonomous iteration stays within settled direction, resources and per-job bounds, with no default aggregate task cap. Machine/E2E checks and warranted independent review supply current proof; final acceptance stays human-owned. Diagnose repeated/broken verification through `systematic-investigation` before resuming with a changed, supported approach. AFK requires verified isolation, resumable state, bounds, cancellation and cleanup.

For multiple contributors/sessions, restore [persistent coordination](team-operating-model/references/persistent-coordination.md) before role task sources: immutable task/role + session binding → scoped `memory-techniques` records/approved plan → bounded `subagent-dispatch` → direction-settled joint plan/authorized execution → append checkpoints after every completed/interrupted slice. Deliberation is optional within a real team; never simulated. [Phased delivery](team-operating-model/references/phased-delivery.md) is independently usable without team activation; use its milestone packet/feedback decisions only for phased work. Roadmaps are for multiple milestones, not every task.

### Intent and Input Assurance

`working-principles` [source integrity](working-principles/references/source-integrity.md)
supports the original-source walkthrough; `code-craft`
[code-intent fit](code-craft/references/code-intent-fit.md) diagnoses patch/refactor
choices; `team-operating-model` [intent assurance](team-operating-model/references/intent-assurance.md)
owns the compact exception/probe handoff. Existing dedicated conformance and critical
behavior checks supply evidence, not new approval rights. `reviewer`
[calibration](reviewer/references/calibration.md) checks reviewer changes before
increased reliance; `project-foundation` [context integrity](project-foundation/references/context-integrity.md)
owns affected source/status/consumer reconciliation, not a custom link checker. Human findings/limits:
[Intent assurance](../docs/agentic-qa/intent-assurance/README.md).

### Delegated Execution

Every named/fallback/dynamic worker or external-node launch uses `subagent-dispatch` and its [worker contract](subagent-dispatch/references/worker-contract.md): scope, output/evidence, READ/WRITE/RUN/network limits, stops and accessible guidance discovery. Workers use `working-principles` themselves; optional hints/references are not inherited parent guidance. Main agents use the same style router; mechanical tasks may use baseline only. When warranted, team deliberation uses separately executed complementary workers (`/swarm`/`/party-mode` only where available); missing permitted workers blocks.

### Plan / Architecture Challenge (Deliberation-Based)

Direction-eligible delegated planner/architect → **separate different-provider-family** reviewer `pragmatic-triage` (justify complexity by probability × impact) → `adversarial` challenge of surviving assumptions → primary's Material Decision Brief. The producer must not simulate its own challenger. This check is additional to direction settlement.

### Review / Audit Cross-Validation

Delegated reviewer/auditor/scanner findings are claims, not facts: independent different-provider-family reviewer `findings-skeptic` checks evidence/context/severity; `pragmatic-triage` challenges defensive complexity when proposed. Present only verified findings at calibrated severity; filter false positives before acting.

### Strategic Human Interaction (Cross-Cutting)

`systematic-investigation`, `brainstorming` or any domain owner → `game-theory` **only when interdependent human responses materially affect the outcome**. Supply observations/rival causes or candidate changes; use its short path before optional deep patterns. It owns choice/information/incentive reconstruction, response traces and rule comparisons; return evidence-labelled hypotheses, options, distributional effects, disconfirmers and unknowns **to the same owner**, which retains workflow, values, evidence gates and authority. No automatic panel, recursion, outreach or implementation. Decision consultation is not strategic analysis. `working-principles` selects this method via its catalog; its incentives-and-constraints reference remains the physical/contingent/value-context bridge, not a competing operational method.

## Composition Patterns

### Investigation → Fix → Review

Unfamiliar area → `codebase-exploration`; observed failure → `systematic-investigation`; supported root cause → `code-craft` working fix → separate `code-maintainability` report → warranted correctness/safety `reviewer`, not mandatory style polish. Investigation may instead hand root-cause findings to `brainstorming` for options or `skill-author` for recurring governance failures.

### Feature Implementation

Shallow research until active decision/slice/non-deferrable boundaries are clear → settle consequential behavior/trust/state/consumer contracts (architecture/planning only as needed) → `code-craft` verifies one active slice → separate maintainability assessment → warranted contract review → evidence/feedback. Use milestone packets and canonical feedback decisions only for phased delivery; reviewer feedback can return to feature planning.

### Working First → Assess Now → Refine Later

After working verification, the primary dispatches `code-maintainability` with outcome, revision/files, checks, shortcuts and authorized record destination. Assessment is report-only (primary persists if assessor cannot); missing delegation/recording is pending, never simulated. Apply selected suggestions only after usefulness and explicit bounded user approval; revalidate stale reports, recheck behavior and update the record, then close. No automatic reassessment except request/new invalidating evidence; changed boundaries/scope return to primary. Safety/correctness/integrity/isolation/required compatibility are defects, not deferrable polish. Specs/mechanical edits do not trigger assessment. `code-craft` owns implementation/testing/navigation/language/pattern libraries; assessors own local SOLID/readability/flow-cost methods, not an upfront implementation gate.

### Structural Integrity Across Agents

[Architecture structural integrity](architecture-design/references/structural-integrity.md) governs consequential placement/dependency changes; [source tracing](codebase-exploration/references/structural-tracing.md) supplies current source/LSP evidence; [memory source maps](memory-techniques/references/source-maps.md) optionally capture it. Implementers respect ownership/trust/state/consumer boundaries; dispatch carries constraints/actual deltas; team owns aggregate acceptance, reviewer warranted correctness/safety, maintainability optional later refinement. No mandatory extra map/store.

### UI/UX Implementation

`ui-ux` discovery→journeys→layout→states→style→code→verify under UX-SPEC → `code-craft` Phase 6 implementation/verification and later separate assessment → reviewer security for input/auth/action boundaries → optional Deep-track Phase 7 `web-qa-audit`. Generative UI stays within this owner: load [generative UI](ui-ux/references/generative-ui.md) and [OpenUI](ui-ux/references/openui.md) only when model-composed interfaces need catalog/prompt/streaming/provenance/action contracts. Ordinary UI does not take that branch.

### Developer Experience

`developer-experience` owns developer-task friction, scoped coverage and discoverability across configuration, invocation, project/module views, optional diagnostics, replay/recovery and conventions. `codebase-exploration` owns source tracing; `architecture-design` owns structural interpretation and changed responsibility/dependency contracts; DX selects and labels useful views, not a second C4 method. `systematic-investigation` owns root causes; `code-craft` implements settled changes; `code-maintainability` assesses working-code refinements without automatic cleanup. `project-foundation` owns foundation/pack bootstrap, not every task entry point. Replay specialization goes to `ml-training`, `distributed-systems-operations` or `database-access` as warranted; `doc-craft` presents substantial human-facing material. No required DX-SPEC, task runner, graph platform or telemetry deployment; missing evidence limits the affected claim, never implies install/export/refactor authority.

### Data Story → Visual → Illustration

`data-storytelling` derives evidence, answer-first narrative and chart needs → `illustration-craft` only beyond standard charts/Mermaid → optional high-stakes editorial/design-rigor review. For architecture, `architecture-design` maps systems/trade-offs first; add storytelling for nontechnical/decision audiences and bespoke illustration only beyond Mermaid/C4. Finished illustrations can hand to editorial review.

### Scientific Research & Ideation

`research-ideation` owns modality audit + three-angle hypothesis tournament → adversarial critique/literature → falsifiable proposal and Colab/Marimo notebook blueprint, replacing production TDD/slicing. Warranted scientific review checks controls/statistics/falsifiability before laboratory commitment; ideation grants no compute/lab authority.

### ML Experiment Execution and Recovery

Hypotheses from `research-ideation` when needed → `ml-training` split provenance, update/event schedules, preflight/retention before launch (existing runs: recovery, not automatic rerun) → investigate evaluation/callback/serialization/logging failures before repair → `code-craft` for non-trivial pipeline changes → `data-storytelling` measured split/checkpoint/coverage-aware results. Snapshots are not trajectories.

### Distributed Runtime and State Integration

Already-chosen compute/storage/sync/consensus platform → `distributed-systems-operations` actual target/version, invariants, placement/resources, commit/retry/recovery and verified bounded integration before scale → `code-craft` adapters (`database-access` for transactional sink/deduplication). `ml-training` retains model split/schedule/metric/checkpoint contracts. Investigate stalls/failures; review warranted resource/security/correctness boundaries. Undecided stack → architecture selection; AI-agent delegation → `subagent-dispatch`, not distributed code-task operations. No implicit launch/mutation/transfer/spend/sign authority.

### Documentation Craftsmanship

Domain specification owner → `doc-craft` audience/format/layering/abstraction/visual rhythm → `mermaid-validation` for diagrams (render SVG/PNG for Typst, not diagram source as the visual) → warranted editorial review. Preserve native Markdown consumers; comprehensive human-facing detail uses Typst/PDF. Specs can hand directly to independent semantic/editorial review; internal plans/phase specs/consensus tracking go to `memory-techniques`, not document publishing.

### Browser Automation

Explore unfamiliar site structure before authoring domain skills → `cdp-browser-automation` terminal-browser-first live interaction/repro/verification; Chrome/CDP only when explicitly requested or a demonstrated gap requires it. Reviewer security for auth/cookies/sensitive data.

### Web QA Audit

Heuristic `reviewer` black-box QA identifies live-evidence need → `web-qa-audit` scope/scenarios/evidence/materialization (grooming/run-card approval before browser-audit path) → `cdp-browser-automation` mechanics → review findings/plans as warranted. Preserve requested browser/trace coverage, not silent substitution. **Only after machine evidence and for non-dev/business/release-owner readers**, switch within QA to stakeholder-report projection (YAML/MD→Excel/PDF/static HTML); only after projection gates, optionally use high-stakes `data-storytelling`. Do not take these reporting branches for engineering-only checks/audits.

### Project Foundation (Bootstrap, Materialize, Audit/Evolve)

`project-foundation` Bootstrap / Audit-Evolve / Materialize **full resolvable skill trees, not index stubs** → exploration if domain/glossary mapping needed → architecture when complex → platform-specific `devsecops` → review generated governance after bootstrap/major evolution. Missing skills/FOUNDATION.md or stale architecture/glossary → Audit/Evolve; core pack materialized → drift audit. Architecture mapping can update GLOSSARY through foundation; frontend foundation can hand to `ui-ux` DESIGN.md setup. Written architecture documents → `reviewer` design-rigor lens for design discipline.

### DevSecOps Hardening

Existing pipeline/security posture → `devsecops` CI/CD, secrets/dependencies/SAST/IaC/audit scanning and integration → `code-craft` remediation → reviewer security verification. Project bootstrap precedes hardening, not the reverse.

### Strategic Positioning via OSINT

`strategic-osint` translates public target/organization/market signals to priorities and actions, not candidate screening (`talent-screening`) → `brainstorming` options or settled product intent → needed technical/behavior owner → editorial/adversarial narrative challenge. Signals/options ready for capital allocation/diligence → `investment-assessment`.

### Database Design → Database Access Implementation

`db-design` schema/migrations/typed mapping → `database-access` repositories/adapters, session lifecycle, write/test contracts → `code-craft` verified implementation → reviewer security (parameterization/injection/entity exposure). If access boundaries/facade/capabilities are undecided, `architecture-design` settles them first → access implementation → reviewer design-rigor boundary check. DB design ER diagrams → `mermaid-validation`.

### Analytical Data Processing & Pipelines (Composable Data Stack)

`architecture-design` data topology, embedded DuckDB vs warehouse and Ibis query boundary → `code-craft` Ibis+DuckDB pipeline (`python-data-stack.md`) → `data-storytelling` out-of-core profiling/signals → reviewer memory safety, pushdown/lazy streaming rather than ballooning Pandas or isolated Polars lock-in. Storytelling can return programmatic extraction to code-craft; architecture MCP/tool-server bootstrap/router/endpoints/middleware/contracts likewise hands settled implementation to code-craft.

### Domain Knowledge Curation

`domain-curation` concrete task→credible lineage→conditional practitioner judgment→representative/boundary checks→brief. Add investigation for failures, consultation for choices, review for evidence; scientific next outcomes use `research-ideation`, reader-ready material `doc-craft`, requested retention `memory-techniques`. Package via `skill-author` only when recurring workflow, critical evidence and real task-attempt limits justify it; otherwise retain the brief. Already-grounded authoring skips acquisition.

### Skill Authoring & Maintenance

`skill-author` Workflow A create/modify or B audit/failure review → foundation for missing foundational files, exploration for unknown code, domain-curation for ungrounded practitioner/domain advice → independent adversarial review. Audit gaps can return B→A; new registered skills go A→B maintenance rotation, not deferred initial discovery. Audit conclusions also need challenge.

## Handoff Matrix

The composition patterns above are the canonical domain handoffs; this matrix covers cross-domain transitions not repeated there. Triggers, not a mandatory pipeline, select each edge.

| From | To | Trigger / retained boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Team deliberation | `code-craft` | Direction settled and implementation authorized |
| Team deliberation ↔ `model-benchmarking` | Model selection ↔ team deliberation | Optimize architecture-specific assignments; return selected models for deliberation |
| `model-benchmarking` | `architecture-design` | Verified token costs/limits inform technical trade-offs |
| `talent-screening` | `reviewer` editorial | Candidate evaluation report ready for peer review |
| `brainstorming` | `investment-assessment` | Options framed; diligence/allocation needed |
| `investment-assessment` | Team finance deliberation / reviewer `investment-memo` | Draft memo, high-stakes allocation or independent suitability/regime challenge; finance personas in `team-operating-model/references/personas/finance/` via `discover-personas.sh` |
| Reviewer `investment-memo` | `investment-assessment` | Failed gates require revised size/allocation; credit/bonds remain a module, not another default owner |
| Any skill / team / document work | `memory-techniques` Capture | Requested handoff/context save or team slice checkpoint; internal execution plans/phase specs/consensus belong here |
| `memory-techniques` Recall | Requesting skill | Restore session/task progress before resuming |
| Any skill | `memory-techniques` Structure | Authorized progressive-disclosure reorganization of docs/modules |
| Any skill | `memory-techniques` Consolidate via fresh subagent | Explicit memory consolidation/dream-cycle/notes-review request; accepted-task pass requires recorded user acceptance and remains report-only |
| Memory consolidation report | Approved memory application / Evict | Subsequent explicit approval before long-term writes, markers, archive or eviction; unavailable delegation does not silently authorize substitution; size limits flag an approval-gated eviction proposal |
| Team / subagent dispatch | Each other as needed | Fresh/replacement bounded task-role dispatch; separately executed team deliberation when warranted, never simulated fallback |
| Any implementation skill | `reviewer` | Requested or warranted independent review, not automatic optional refinement |
| Any domain skill | Team delivery | Authorized outcome needs a real-team implement/evaluate/correct loop; never use activation to continue solo |

